IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, section 104 -- THE ORGANIZATION MEETING OF
-- THE DIRECTORS. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs.

§ `s 104 Organization meeting`

§§ `s 104(2) Exception`

-- out of range: section 185(4) (piece cb4); out of range: section 187(4) (piece cb4)
-- src:1224 | Exception
-- src:1225 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a body corporate to which a certificate of amalgamation has been issued under subsection 185(4) or to which a certificate of continuance has been issued under subsection 187(4).
@ref CBCA s 104(2) (src:1224-1225)
GIVEN `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 104(1) does not apply to the body corporate within s 104(2)` MEANS
        `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)`
    OR  `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)`

§§ `s 104(1) Organization meeting`

-- out of range: section 185(4) (piece cb4); out of range: section 187(4) (piece cb4)
-- src:1215 | Organization meeting
-- src:1216 | 104 (1) After issue of the certificate of incorporation, a meeting of the directors of the corporation shall be held at which the directors may
@ref CBCA s 104(1) (src:1215-1216)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a meeting of the directors must be held within s 104(1)` MEANS
        `the certificate of incorporation has been issued`
    AND (NOT `subsection 104(1) does not apply to the body corporate within s 104(2)`
                 `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)`
                 `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)`)

-- src:1215 | Organization meeting
-- src:1216 | 104 (1) After issue of the certificate of incorporation, a meeting of the directors of the corporation shall be held at which the directors may
-- src:1217 | (a) make by-laws;
-- src:1218 | (b) adopt forms of security certificates and corporate records;
-- src:1219 | (c) authorize the issue of securities;
-- src:1220 | (d) appoint officers;
-- src:1221 | (e) appoint an auditor to hold office until the first annual meeting of shareholders;
-- src:1222 | (f) make banking arrangements; and
-- src:1223 | (g) transact any other business.
@ref CBCA s 104(1) (src:1215-1223)
DECLARE `Business the directors may transact at the organization meeting` IS ONE OF
    `making by-laws`
    `adopting forms of security certificates and corporate records`
    `authorizing the issue of securities`
    `appointing officers`
    `appointing an auditor to hold office until the first annual meeting of shareholders`
    `making banking arrangements`
    `transacting any other business`

-- NOTHING: no organization meeting is required of this body corporate.
-- out of range: section 185(4) (piece cb4); out of range: section 187(4) (piece cb4)
-- src:1215 | Organization meeting
-- src:1216 | 104 (1) After issue of the certificate of incorporation, a meeting of the directors of the corporation shall be held at which the directors may
-- src:1217 | (a) make by-laws;
-- src:1218 | (b) adopt forms of security certificates and corporate records;
-- src:1219 | (c) authorize the issue of securities;
-- src:1220 | (d) appoint officers;
-- src:1221 | (e) appoint an auditor to hold office until the first annual meeting of shareholders;
-- src:1222 | (f) make banking arrangements; and
-- src:1223 | (g) transact any other business.
@ref CBCA s 104(1) (src:1215-1223)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Business the directors may transact at the organization meeting`)
`the business the directors may transact at the organization meeting within s 104(1)` MEANS
    IF `a meeting of the directors must be held within s 104(1)`
           `the certificate of incorporation has been issued`
           `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 185(4)`
           `a certificate of continuance has been issued to the body corporate under subsection 187(4)`
    THEN JUST (LIST `making by-laws`,
                    `adopting forms of security certificates and corporate records`,
                    `authorizing the issue of securities`,
                    `appointing officers`,
                    `appointing an auditor to hold office until the first annual meeting of shareholders`,
                    `making banking arrangements`,
                    `transacting any other business`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 104(3) Calling meeting`

-- src:1226 | Calling meeting
-- src:1227 | (3) An incorporator or a director may call the meeting of directors referred to in subsection (1) by giving not less than five days notice thereof by mail to each director, stating the time and place of the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 104(3) (src:1226-1227)
GIVEN `the person is an incorporator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may call the meeting within s 104(3)` MEANS
        `the person is an incorporator`
    OR  `the person is a director`

-- "Not less than five days notice ... by mail to each director, stating the time and place".
-- src:1226 | Calling meeting
-- src:1227 | (3) An incorporator or a director may call the meeting of directors referred to in subsection (1) by giving not less than five days notice thereof by mail to each director, stating the time and place of the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 104(3) (src:1226-1227)
GIVEN `the person is an incorporator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by mail to each director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the time and place of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meeting is called as required within s 104(3)` MEANS
        `the person may call the meeting within s 104(3)` `the person is an incorporator` `the person is a director`
    AND `the notice is given by mail to each director`
    AND `the notice states the time and place of the meeting`
    AND `the number of days of notice given` AT LEAST 5
